  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of siting, scale, mass and design, would be a bulky, discordant addition which would&nbsp;would appear overly dominant and not have regard to the original built form of the host dwelling and the area. The proposal would introduce a massing at roof level which would be insubordinate to the dwelling. Its design does not reflect the character of the area. This would cause unacceptable harm to the character and appearance of the original dwelling and surrounding area. The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals have regard to the existing character: National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024) Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
